<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joseph Frederick Wallet DesBarres</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1721–1824</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joseph Frederick Wallet DesBarres was a Swiss-born military engineer and cartographer whose Atlantic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neptune">Neptune</a> charted the coasts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. In 1784 he became the first lieutenant governor of the new Colony of Cape Breton Island and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia">Sydney</a> as its capital in 1785. He later governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-edward-island">Prince Edward Island</a> and lived to the age of 102.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joseph-frederick-wallet-desbarres.jpg" alt="Joseph Frederick Wallet DesBarres" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, credited to James Peachey · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WalletDesBarres2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
